# Cursor rules for Sakura & Sawasdee

Read `CLAUDE.md` at the project root before writing any code. It is the project
constitution and overrides anything that conflicts with it.

Quick reference — the rules most often broken:

1. `src/learning/` must not import from `game/`, `ui/`, Phaser or React. Pure logic only.
2. `src/game/` must not import React. `src/ui/` must not import Phaser at runtime
   (`import type` and dynamic `import()` are fine).
3. Phaser and React communicate ONLY through `src/state/eventBus.ts` and Zustand stores.
4. No file over 300 lines. No `any`. No `@ts-ignore`.
5. Colours come from `src/game/palette.ts`. Never hardcode a hex value.
   Never use pure black or pure white.
6. Never hardcode Thai or Japanese text in code — it lives in `src/content/` or `src/i18n/`.
7. Every function in `src/learning/` needs a Vitest unit test.
8. Never write a TODO, placeholder or mock without saying so explicitly in your reply.

Design pillars every feature must satisfy:

- **Always gentle** — wrong answers must not punish; fleeing always works
- **Every mechanic teaches** — no minigame unrelated to language
- **Living pastel** — every scene has something always in motion
- **Comprehensible from day one** — dialogue adapts to known words
- **Culture as mechanic** — politeness, keigo and tones are real systems

Build order lives in `docs/02_Prompt_Pack.md`. Do not skip phases.
